  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "TLS: add new ALPS extension codepoint",
  "description": "BoringSSL switched to a new ALPS codepoint to allow adding more data in the ACCEPT_CH HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 frame.\n\nThe ALPS codepoint changes from 17513 to 17613.\n\nFeature announcement: https://chromestatus.com/feature/5149147365900288\nRelevant code: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/master/include/openssl/tls1.h?pli=1#112\n\nFor backward-compatibility, the previous codepoint has been renamed to \"application_settings_old\", following the already existing logic for the \"channel_id_old\" extension.\n\nI also attach a pcapng with 2 Client Hellos with both codepoints: one collected from Chromium 136 and the other from Chromium 120.\n[new_alps.pcapng](/uploads/da661c15f54394e54882442b338b6f2a/new_alps.pcapng)",
